
PACE Scorecard - 2027
Shopify Global Accounts PACE Performance Scoring & Relative Ranking

A BIDS and Operations guide to balanced scorecard

1. Purpose

Definition: PACE is a standardized performance scoring framework designed to measure both:
1. Absolute Performance — how well a teammate performs against the required account target.
2. Relative Performance — how the teammate performs compared with other teammates doing comparable work.
Problem Addressed: PACE prevents traditional population-based quartiling from creating misleading results.
Under traditional quartiling, teammates can be placed into higher quartiles simply because they perform better than their peers, even when the entire population is below target.
Solution: PACE solves this by applying a Target Gate before relative ranking is used to differentiate performance.
Core principle: First, meet the standard. Then, show how far above the standard you perform
2. PACE Philosophy

PACE is not intended to identify a winner simply by ranking teammates against one another.
It is intended to answer two questions:
1. Are you meeting the account standard measured through absolute performance?
2. How strong is your performance compared with your qualified peers measured through relative performance?
Standard Scoring Model:


70% Absolute Performance + 30% Relative Performance
Rationale:


Absolute performance has greater weight because the account target represents the minimum required standard.
Relative performance adds differentiation among teammates without allowing population ranking to replace the account standard.
