5. Target Gate

The Target Gate is the most important control in PACE.
Rule: Relative ranking cannot compensate for failure to meet the required KPI target.
Example:


Smiley Target = 81%
A teammate with 79% Smiley may rank better than many peers.
They are still below the required Smiley target.
Therefore, relative ranking cannot automatically classify that teammate as an upper-band performer.
Key Takeaway: Being better than someone who is also below target does not mean you are meeting the standard.
