7. Step 1 — Calculate Attainment

Target Factor measures how actual performance compares with the target.
Higher-is-better KPIs:


Smiley
AFTR
Quality
Formula: Attainment = Actual ÷ Target


Example:


Smiley Actual = 85%
Smiley Target = 81%
85 ÷ 81 = 1.049
The teammate is performing at approximately 104.9% of target.
Lower-is-better KPIs:


AHT
Formula: Attainment = Target ÷ Actual


Example:


AHT Target = 500 seconds
AHT Actual = 480 seconds
500 ÷ 480 = 1.042
The teammate is performing at approximately 104.2% of target.
8. Direction Standardization

BIDS must always ensure: A higher attainment means better performance.
Standardization Rules:


Smiley: Higher actual = better attainment.
AFTR: Higher actual = better attainment.
Quality: Higher actual = better attainment.
AHT: Lower actual = better attainment.
This standardization is required before relative ranking is calculated.
