28. Tie Handling

Reporting must define a consistent approach when teammates have identical KPI results.
Recommended approach: "teammates with identical performance values should receive the same rank/percentile treatment."
The system must not arbitrarily assign different rankings to identical KPI results.
The selected percentile methodology must be documented in the reporting logic.
29. Missing Data

teammates should not receive an artificial score when a KPI does not have sufficient valid data.
Examples:


Insufficient survey responses
Insufficient contact volume
No Quality evaluations
Invalid or missing production data
Reporting should:


Identify the missing KPI.
Apply the approved minimum-data rule.
Exclude the teammate from relative ranking for that KPI when appropriate.
Flag the record.
Prevent an invalid score from influencing the overall PACE.
