37. Simple Explanation for a Frontline Agent

PACE can be explained in five sentences:
"PACE looks at four things: Smiley, AHT, AFTR and Quality.
First, we check whether you meet the target for each KPI.
Then we compare your performance with people doing similar work.
Your final score is 70% based on performance against target and 30% based on your position among your peers.
You cannot become a Peak performer simply because you rank well if you are still below the required target."
38. PACE Formula Summary

Target Factor:


Higher is better: "Actual ÷ Target"
Lower is better: "Target ÷ Actual"
Relative Score:


"100 − Reverse Percentile"
Final KPI Score:


"Absolute Score × 70% + Relative Score × 30%"
Overall Score:


"Smiley × 30% + Quality × 30% + AFTR × 25% + AHT × 15%"
Final Classification:


"Overall Score + Target Gates + PACE Guardrails"
